n paper on the square-energy conjecture, we reduce the theorem to a Motzkin--Straus inequality for doubly nonnegative matrices, which we prove via a local inverse-probability estimate for the Caro--Wei greedy algorithm on the complement.\n\n## Papers by Yinchen Liu\n\n7 paper(s) by this author · All BibTeX\n\n2026-08-09\n\nYinchen Liu, Quanyu Tang\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nThe $Δ$-Conjecture for CIS $d$-Graphs\n\nWe prove the $Δ$-conjecture, which dates back to Gurvich's 1978 thesis. Specifically, let the edges of a complete graph be colored with colors $1,\\ldots,d$, and for each $i$ let $G_i$ be the graph formed by the edges of color $i$. We prove that if every choice of a maximal stable set $S_i$ of $G_i$, one for each $i\\in[d]$, has nonempty intersection, then the coloring contains no rainbow triangle.\n\n2026-07-20\n\nYinchen Liu, Quanyu Tang, Shengtong Zhang\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nThe positive and negative square-energy conjecture\n\nLet $s^+(G)$ and $s^-(G)$ denote the sums of the squares of the positive and negative adjacency eigenvalues of a graph $G$, respectively. We prove the conjecture of Elphick, Farber, Goldberg, and Wocjan that every connected graph $G$ on $n$ vertices satisfies $$ \\min\\{s^+(G),s^-(G)\\}\\ge n-1. $$ The proof introduces a new framework for square-energy estimates, in which the Hadamard squares of positive semidefinite matrices that encode these spectral quantities are relaxed to the full doubly nonnegative cone.\n\ngraph positive semidefinite matrix connected graph\n\n2026-07-20\n\nYinchen Liu, Quanyu Tang, Shengtong Zhang\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nA positive square-energy strengthening of Turán's theorem\n\nLet $G$ be an $n$-vertex graph with clique number $ω(G)$, and let $s^+(G)$ denote the sum of the squared positive adjacency eigenvalues. We prove that $$ \\sqrt{s^+(G)}\\le\\left(1-\\frac{1}{ω(G)}\\right)n. $$ This strengthens Wilf's classical spectral Turán theorem and resolves a conjecture of Elphick and Wocjan. Adopting the relaxation of our companion paper on the square-energy conjecture, we reduce the theorem to a Motzkin--Straus inequality for doubly nonnegative matrices, which we prove via a local inverse-probability estimate for the Caro--Wei greedy algorithm on the complement.\n\nclique number graph turan theorem\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPositive and Negative Square Energies of $2$-Connected Graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04069)\nciteturn5academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Title: Positive and Negative Square Energies of $2$-Connected Graphs ... Recently, Liu, Tang, and Zhang proved the conjecture of Elphick, Farber, Goldberg, and Wocjan that every connected graph $G$ of order $n$ satisfies $ \\min\\{s^+(G), s^-(G)\\} \\ge n-1. $ For positive square energy, we strengthen this result by showing that every $2$-connected graph $G$ of order $n$ which is not a cycle satisfies $s^+(G)\\ge n$.\nTitle: Positive and Negative Square Energies of $2$-Connected Graphs\nAuthors: S. Akbari, Fu-Tao Hu, Ya-Yang Liu\nDate: Thu Sep  3 16:42:09 2026\n\nLet $G$ be a graph of order $n$, and let $s^+(G)$ and $s^-(G)$ denote the sums of the squares of the positive and negative adjacency eigenvalues of $G$, respectively. Recently, Liu, Tang, and Zhang proved the conjecture of Elphick, Farber, Goldberg, and Wocjan that every connected graph $G$ of order $n$ satisfies $ \\min\\{s^+(G), s^-(G)\\} \\ge n-1. $ For positive square energy, we strengthen this result by showing that every $2$-connected graph $G$ of order $n$ which is not a cycle satisfies $s^+(G)\\ge n$. The formally analogous assertion for $s^-$ is false: the complete graph $K_n$ satisfies $s^-(K_n)=n-1$. We prove a natural counterpart in the triangle-free class: every triangle-free $2$-connected noncycle $G$ satisfies $ \\min\\{s^+(G),s^-(G)\\}>n. $ More generally, it is enough that some maximum-degree vertex of $G$ belongs to no triangle. Together with the exact square energies of cycles, this characterizes the triangle-free $2$-connected graphs for which $s^-(G)\\ge n$; the only exceptions are the cycles $C_{4k+3}$ with $k\\geq1$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSupersaturation: Cliques and Positive Square Energy (https://arxiv.cnoctave.top/pdf/2610.40570)\nciteturn5search13 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Elphick and Wocjan [8, Conjecture 1 and Section 3.1] conjectured the positive square-energy strengthening of Wilf’s bound and proved the triangle-free case. ... Liu, Tang, and Zhang [27] subsequently proved the positive square-energy Turán theorem: every \\(K_{r+1}\\)-free graph satisfies\nThe square energies were studied by Wocjan and Elphick [42], in connection with a spectral lower bound for the chromatic number involving the entire adjacency spectrum. Elphick, Farber, Goldberg, and Wocjan [6] subsequently initiated the systematic study of square energies as graph invariants. Elphick and Wocjan [8, Conjecture 1 and Section 3.1] conjectured the positive square-energy strengthening of Wilf’s bound and proved the triangle-free case. The conjecture and this case also appear in the later work of Elphick, Linz, and Wocjan [7]. Liu, Tang, and Zhang [27] subsequently proved the positive square-energy Turán theorem: every \\(K_{r+1}\\)-free graph satisfies\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{s^+} \\leq \\left(1-\\frac{1}{r}\\right)n.\n\\]\n\nThe equality case was studied by Jayarajan, Kanman, Pragada, and Roy [16]. Our main theorem is a natural extension of the literature of spectral supersaturation to positive square energy. Precisely, we show the following,\n\n**Theorem 1.1.** *For every integer \\(r \\geq 2\\) and every \\(\\varepsilon > 0\\), there exists \\(n_0 = n_0(r,\\varepsilon)\\) such that the following holds. Let \\(G\\) have order \\(n \\geq n_0\\). If*\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{s^+(G)} > \\left(1-\\frac{1}{r}\\right)n,\n\\]\n\n*then*\n\n\\[\nk_{r+1}(G) \\